'' THE SYMBOL TABLE'S RECORDS NEVER MOVE. SymbolTable.SymbolAt / ScopeAt return record
'' addresses that hundreds of call sites keep across a call that declares -- resolving a
'' type that instantiates a generic is enough -- and over a containers.Array each of them
'' dangled when the array grew. On Linux, where a large freed block is unmapped, the
'' compiler crashed in Resolve's generic instantiation (InstantiateProcAt_) and in a
'' module's type aliases (ModuleTypedefsFirst_), on valid programs, depending on file names
'' and the module cache. support/stablevec.ti is the storage now; this pins its invariant:
'' an address taken early is the same address, holding the same bytes, 20,000 appends later.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/stable-store.tiko src/support/stablevec.tiko -i src -o tests/driver/stablestore.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/driver/stablestore.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: records 20000 chunks 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: kept 21 moved 0 wrong 0
